      "side": 1,
      "message": "I didn\u0027t quite understand your last comment. Let me know if this addresses it:\n\nIn one of code iterations, I did not have this do ... while loop. I only armed the timer, then waited for the timer to settle. In that iteration, I \"missed\" a timer event within ~2 hours. Once the timer1 event is missed, the entire OS scheduling stops working.\n\nWhat I mean by \"missing\" a timer event is that the code calls __hw_clock_event_set with a deadline in the future and this function execute to completion, but the timer1 IRQ never fires, and when I look at the system later, timer1 is not enabled (i.e. HPET_Tn_INT_ENB_CNF is unset). In that situation, if I manually fire the IRQ for timer1, then the task scheduling can start running again for a little while.\n\nAdding the extra do...while loop seemed to fix the issue I was seeing where the timer was never enabled and was being \"missed\".",
